---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const title = 'Terms of Service | Mundesha Investments';
const description =
  'The terms that apply when you request a quote or use the Mundesha Investments website. Quotes, scope of work, payment and Namibian law.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/terms">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>TERMS OF SERVICE</h1>
      <p class="lead">The basics of how we quote, work and get paid. Your formal quote or contract always takes precedence.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h3>These terms</h3>
      <p>
        These terms apply when you use this website and when you ask us for a quote. Each job is
        governed by the written quote or contract we issue for it. If the quote and these terms
        differ, the quote wins.
      </p>

      <h3>Quotes</h3>
      <p>
        Every quote states its own validity period and scope. Prices are quoted in Namibian dollars
        (N$) unless stated otherwise. A quote is an offer that becomes binding only when both sides
        agree, in writing or by confirmed instruction to proceed.
      </p>

      <h3>Scope and site access</h3>
      <p>
        We do the work listed in the quote. If the site is not accessible, or if conditions on site
        differ materially from what was described, we will raise it before proceeding and adjust the
        scope and price by agreement. Where we work inside occupied buildings, mines or public
        facilities, we follow the safety and access rules of that site.
      </p>

      <h3>Payment</h3>
      <p>
        Payment terms are stated on each invoice. We may require a deposit or progress payments for
        materials and long jobs. Invoices unpaid by their due date may pause further work until the
        account is settled.
      </p>

      <h3>Warranty and liability</h3>
      <p>
        We stand behind the quality of our work. Installed equipment is covered by the supplier or
        manufacturer warranty that comes with it, and our workmanship is warranted against defects
        for a reasonable period stated in the quote. To the fullest extent allowed by Namibian law,
        we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses. Nothing in these terms limits rights
        you have under Namibian law that cannot be limited.
      </p>

      <h3>Website content</h3>
      <p>
        The project record on this site describes real work done since 2016. Photographs of client
        sites are shown as examples of our work and remain the property of their owners. Client logos
        belong to their respective organisations.
      </p>

      <h3>Law and contact</h3>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Namibia. Questions, disputes or
        notices: {SITE.email}, {SITE.phones[0].display}, {SITE.address}. Effective from 1 October 2026.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
